00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.480
That I tell my patients like, look.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.640
If this continues into tonight

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.540
or gets worse randomly in
the middle of the night

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.080
and you're not sure of what
to do, call our number.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.020
We'll have a resident who's
on call, give you a call back.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.470
They'll help triage of
whether you can wait

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.270
until an urgent care
appointment in the morning.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.430
Or do you have to go to the ER now

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.270
'cause we can talk through the symptoms.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:25.020
We can talk through your history.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.600
You know, in his case,
knowing that he has a history

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.600
of small bowel obstructions, it is wise

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.110
to come in earlier than later.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:33.130
But maybe in someone who, you know,

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.460
ate some food and is having some diarrhea

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.980
and some nausea for four hours,

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.810
maybe they don't need to rush to the ER.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:40.970
Especially if they have access

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:42.210
to a good primary care doctor.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.010
- The first time that it went down

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:48.026
or the nurse tried to get it
down, it went into my lungs.

00:07:48.026 --> 00:07:49.070
(laughs)

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.853
Let me tell you.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.810
Getting a lube covered plastic tube

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.590
shoved in your lungs ain't fun at all.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:00.204
And it was, I felt so bad for the nurse.

00:08:00.204 --> 00:08:02.680
I ended up like, I felt bad for the nurse.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.120
Like, you know, she shoves it down

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.449
