00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.360
I think that was in my lungs.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.500
And she's going like, no
way that was in your lungs.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.010
I'm like lady, I'm not
gonna sue you or anything.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.940
Look, I'm just telling you,
I'm not an expert at the inside

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.590
of my lungs or other fields
that went in my lungs.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:25.430
- Oh my God.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:28.450
STAT portable chest x-ray, please.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:29.320
- You know, if he's coughing

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.070
and he's not able to
tolerate the tube placement,

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.720
it could have gone down the wrong pipe.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.480
After you reached the back of your throat

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:38.160
it splits into your esophagus
and then the wind pipes.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.980
So there is a possibility that
the two may have, you know,

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.160
at least temporarily
gone down the wrong tube.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.204
- Well that's why, right?

00:08:45.204 --> 00:08:47.630
Like one of the parts
of placing an NG tube

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.520
is then listening for the stomach,

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.458
for the lungs and making
sure you don't hear it

00:08:52.458 --> 00:08:55.890
